{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "06ML", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-residual-gerbe}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1b7637cf0c94c379c58b7bff8f8657c836bd99c7f25d3366a4e932102cd12ab1", "source_text": "Residual gerbes", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d20c5faf0dd5c2f3eada6eb0c8814c6f3679cf1d281d90320fc34fd22aee2eb5", "unit_id": "tag:06ML:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06ML", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$x \\in |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0003": "$m_x : \\mathcal{Z}_x \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{Z}_x$", "MATH_0005": "$m_x$", "MATH_0006": "$x$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{Z}_x$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:82bb7e2b3618f3e960e3b42912213db8c53248d24b2f972ec4e1d8dc3aef0580", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:11ac2db9b075790952bb23092d68bdbb9d1f794ade2104204e39043e5ef7b15b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn the Stacks project we would like to define the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>residual gerbe<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nof an algebraic stack <MATH_0001> at a point <MATH_0002>\nto be a monomorphism of algebraic stacks\n<MATH_0003> where <MATH_0004> is a reduced\nalgebraic stack having a unique point which is mapped by <MATH_0005> to <MATH_0006>.\nIt turns out that there are many issues with this notion; existence is not\nclear in general and neither is uniqueness.\nWe resolve the uniqueness issue by imposing a slightly stronger\ncondition on the algebraic stacks <MATH_0007>.\nWe discuss this in more detail by working through a few simple lemmas\nregarding reduced algebraic stacks having a unique point.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4fa798cb8653145704515a12dc807c3d462bbcb32afd2cc9ebd480838ad93ad9", "unit_id": "tag:06ML:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06ML", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0002": "$k$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Spec(k) \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Spec(k') \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0005": "$k'$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-flat-cover-by-field}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f63bb65b4e5bdb1a957893e311d51af93954e6c9df5e531a9d4c14309e06c313", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6a78a4eb6c86cdc9e5cc7a8d914f95db08bc067fc23c1089ad2e37fd5eb8d566", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack. Let <MATH_0002> be a field and let\n<MATH_0003> be surjective and flat. Then any\nmorphism <MATH_0004> where <MATH_0005> is a field is\nsurjective and flat.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:068024d6cbcecc0120af9f64f05cfc433dea2a498e0e8ebf835a025400e9c952", "unit_id": "tag:06MM:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06ML", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nT \\ar[d] \\ar[r] & \\Spec(k) \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\Spec(k') \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{Z}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$T \\to \\Spec(k')$", "MATH_0003": "$T$", "MATH_0004": "$T \\to \\Spec(k)$", "MATH_0005": "$k$", "MATH_0006": "$T \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Spec(k') \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0008": "$|\\mathcal{Z}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-flat-permanence}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{section-properties-morphisms}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4db5eee286ee7a54c6db8214e3dc926837b546ac3357aca84c5269e48725cb08", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a4986f64bc80b639c5c15e927872450a3f4c3e76b1a1ce252db89c35df5c017e", "source_text": "Consider the fibre square\n<MATH_0001>\nNote that <MATH_0002> is flat and surjective hence <MATH_0003>\nis not empty. On the other hand <MATH_0004> is flat as\n<MATH_0005> is a field. Hence <MATH_0006> is flat and surjective.\nIt follows from\nMorphisms of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0001>\n(via the discussion in\nSection <REF_0002>)\nthat <MATH_0007> is flat. It is clear that it\nis surjective as by assumption <MATH_0008> is a singleton.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1bc082d8e507678efeff433897187b161337b0c7305048b4b1a5cd31dd6832db", "unit_id": "tag:06MM:proof"}
